gta online gets a big update ubisoft is  on a canceling and delaying spree plus  dragon ball the breakers finally gets a  release date  as development on gta 6 progresses  rockstar continues to support gta online  with significant updates the newest of  these is criminal enterprises a free  expansion coming july 26th a line from  the expansion's description reads quote  the southern san andreas economy is in  crisis gas prices have spiked to their  highest level in decades retail supply  chains are in turmoil and to top it all  off a ferocious heatwave is gripping the  state sounds oddly familiar in the  expansion you will take on a new mission  called operation paper trail as an agent  of the international affairs agency to  see if the dugan petrochemical family  are deliberately manipulating the fuel  market the criminal enterprises  expansion is also described as a  sweeping update that kicks off a series  of additions bringing new modes vehicles  collectibles and special events to the  game throughout the rest of the summer  any gta online player who owns an  executive office will find a new staff  manager lupe who can help you find  special cargo additionally executives  can now take on new missions there are  also new clubhouse contracts for players  who have a clubhouse with the custom  bike shop elsewhere the criminal  enterprises expansion adds more resupply  missions that challenges players to rob  targets to get more gear for nightclub  owners there is a new contract to take  on to acquire new goods and wares beyond  all of this rockstar says that fans  should keep an eye out for a  comprehensive list of new gameplay and  experience improvements across all of  gta online rockstar will share further  details on the gameplay and balance  changes of criminal enterprises on july  26th when the expansion arrives and as  usual this update is coming to ps5 4  xbox one series x and s and pc but not  to playstation 3 and xbox 360. in other  news bandai namco has confirmed dragon  ball the breakers will release on  october 14th the game pits seven  survivors non-powered human characters  against one player controlled by iconic  villains the game pits seven survivors  non-player human characters against one  player controlling iconic villains or  raiders from across the dragon ball  universe the seven must survive until  the end of the match using items and  perks against the villain who wins by  eliminating all other players a network  test for dragon ball the breakers was  also confirmed which will take place on  august 5th and 6th across four sessions  the times for these are as follows i'm  only reading off the eastern times but i  will include all in the description  below august 5th from 10 p.m eastern to  2 a.m eastern august 6th from 8 a.m 2 12  p.m 2 p.m to 6 p.m and 10 pm to 2 am  switching gears to avatar frontiers of  pandora announced today as part of its  earnings briefing ubisoft revealed the  new avatar game will not launch on  schedule and is now aiming for release  next fiscal year which begins april 1st  2023 and ends on june 30th 2024 and  frontiers of pandora isn't the only  ubisoft game being delayed as it was  also confirmed that a smaller  unannounced premium game has shifted to  next fiscal year as well aside from the  delays ubisoft also revealed that two  other unannounced games have been  cancelled as well as splinter cell vr  and ghost recon frontlines the good news  though is that the future of assassin's  creed will be revealed during an event  this september but alright on a scale of  one to ten let me know how excited you  are for this avatar game i haven't  really heard anyone talking about it  doesn't seem like the hype is way up  there so i'm dying to know what your  feelings are about it and i'll see you  tomorrow
 

